[statement]
A character device declaring a size, its body holding two headers. POSIX
leaves a device's size unspecified and stores no data after it. The reference
readers read no data and list the two headers as members; some Rust readers
read them as data. In Strict, ferrotape refuses the archive; in Compatible,
it reads the device with no data, and the two members after it.

[archive]
header name=t3 typeflag=3 size=1024
header name=s31
header name=s32
header name=tail
data "hello\n"
end

[verdict]
strict: refused SizeWithoutData at 0
compatible: read

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=c path=t3 device=0,0 mode=0o644
member listed=- path=s31 size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
member listed=- path=s32 size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
member listed=- path=tail size=6 mode=0o644 data="hello\n"
exit 0

